# CampusPulse Admin Implementation Report

The Admin dashboard has been fully fleshed out with working sub-pages, safe APIs, and proper authorization constraints.

## 1. Pages Created
The following new React components were created and wired into `App.tsx` following the existing styling (cards, tables, Lucide icons, responsive modals):
- `AdminUsers.tsx` (`/admin/users`)
- `AdminDepartments.tsx` (`/admin/departments`)
- `AdminSubjects.tsx` (`/admin/subjects`)
- `AdminClasses.tsx` (`/admin/classes`)
- `AdminAnnouncements.tsx` (`/admin/announcements`)

## 2. APIs Reused vs Added
**Reused:**
- `GET /departments`, `GET /subjects`, `GET /announcements`, `GET /faculties` (for dropdowns)

**Added (Admin Only):**
- **Users**: `GET /admin/users` (dynamically resolves names and departments from Student/Faculty profiles), `PATCH /admin/users/{user_id}/status`
- **Departments**: `POST /departments`, `PUT /departments/{id}`, `DELETE /departments/{id}` (protected by active student constraint)
- **Subjects**: `POST /subjects`, `PUT /subjects/{id}`, `DELETE /subjects/{id}`
- **Announcements**: `POST /announcements`, `PUT /announcements/{id}`, `DELETE /announcements/{id}`
- **Classes**: `GET /admin/classes` (dynamically groups active students by Department, Year, and Semester — avoiding the need for a duplicate model/table).

## 3. Database Models Reused
- **No SQLite reset** or destruction of data was performed.
- Existing models (`User`, `Department`, `Subject`, `Announcement`, `Student`) were fully reused without creating duplicate tables.

## 4. Admin Authorization Verified
- Every single new backend endpoint checks `current_user.role != "ADMIN"`.
- If a Student or Faculty attempts to make POST/PUT/DELETE calls to these endpoints, the server returns a secure `403 Not authorized` response.
- Frontend routes are shielded by the existing `ProtectedRoute` logic with `allowedRoles={['ADMIN']}`.

## 5. CRUD Operations Implemented
- **Users**: Read, toggle active status (deactivate).
- **Departments**: Full Create, Read, Update, Delete (Safe delete constraint added).
- **Subjects**: Full Create, Read, Update, Delete.
- **Classes**: Read-only (Derived dynamically from active student enrollments per requirements).
- **Announcements**: Full Create, Read, Update, Delete.

## 6. Regression Testing
- Ran frontend TypeScript build checks (`tsc --noEmit`) to verify no missing imports, type errors, or broken route declarations.
- Re-loaded the Backend router to ensure no cyclical imports or missing references.
- Verified that previously fixed API endpoints for Student/Faculty functionality remain fully intact and operational.

## Remaining Limitations
- **Deleting constraints**: Currently, deleting a Department prevents deletion if there are active students. It does not check for active Subjects/Faculty for brevity, though deleting those would cascade safely in the DB.
- **Class Management**: Assigning faculty to an entire "Class" is inherently tricky when Classes are dynamically grouped by semester, so faculty assignment remains managed at the `Subject` level (which is how the DB is currently architected).
